  "sellingType": "By Private Treaty",
  "description": "Bowe Property is delighted to bring to the market a prime residential development site on the western fringes of Bandon Town, just 32km southwest of Cork City, within one of the most sought after residential locations of Bandon Town, being Old Chapel on the western fringes of the town, within less than 2km of the town centre itself. The lands extend to approximately 5.5 acres and are contained in Folio CK24305 and have the benefit of a recent planning permission, full grant under planning reference no. 25/6896 by Cork County Council for forty dwelling houses, incorporating 5 four bed semi-detached houses, 2 four bed detached houses, 24 three bed semi-detached houses, 2 three bed detached houses as well as 7 two bed semi-detached houses. The proposed development is shovel ready and, in every sense of the word, prime, given its strong location and its fantastic setting. Old Chapel is primarily a residential location on the western fringes of Bandon Town, with Bandon Grammar School nearby, and has been the location of a number of low density, successful residential developments of late, with the location proving itself as a high-demand location amongst buyers of all types. The site has the benefit of not just the attractive planning, but having services all available nearby. The natural topography of the site is very workable, and the demand for the proposed homes is presently very strong amongst all buyer types.\n\n\nA full planning pack and conditions of sale are available from the sole selling agent, Brendan Bowe, on 087 259 4481 or brendan@bowe.ie.",
